{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310747,"nonce":"xC4o00ktkKtWlesDKXDr2KH2cW0=","title":"wasm backend drops a GENERIC-typed operand from string concatenation (`String += x` where x:T) → silently produces empty string. ...","message":"**Discovered 2026-06-14** while fixing nue `GenerationLoop` streaming decode. `StringBuf` silently produced EMPTY strings on the rayzor wasm backend (works on native), so streamed text never appeared. Worked around in nue by using a plain `String` accumulator ([[bugs_wasm_long_gen_string_oom]] decode fix, commit 13519e5). The underlying COMPILER bug remains.\n\n**Minimal isolation (/tmp/sbtest/Iso.hx), each `Box.b:String` starts `\"\"`, append `\"X\"`:**\n| construct | native | wasm |\n|---|---|---|\n| `add\u003cT\u003e(x:T){ b += x; }` (inline) | `X` | **`` (empty)** |\n| `add\u003cT\u003e(x:T){ b += x; }` (non-inline) | `X` | **`` (empty)** |\n| `add(x:String){ b += x; }` | `X` | `X` ✓ |\n| `add(x:String){ b = b + x; }` | `X` | `X` ✓ |\n| `add\u003cT\u003e(x:T){ b += Std.string(x); }` | **`\u003cunknown type 211501057\u003e`** | **`4116`** |\n\n**Root cause (narrowed):** when a string concatenation (`+` / `+=`) has an operand whose static type is a GENERIC parameter `T` (not resolved to `String`), the wasm backend does NOT coerce it to its string value — the operand is dropped and the concat yields empty. `String += \u003cString\u003e` (statically typed) works fine, so the concat machinery itself is OK; the gap is the missing generic→string coercion. Separately, `Std.string(x:T)` is broken on BOTH backends (native emits `\u003cunknown type N\u003e`, wasm emits a raw pointer) — the runtime-type-to-string path doesn't handle a generic-erased value.\n\n**Two candidate fixes:** (a) MONOMORPHIZE generic method instantiations so `add\u003cString\u003e(\"X\")` types `x` as `String` before lowering (then `b += x` is `String += String`, which works) — native already behaves as if it does this for `+=`; the wasm backend doesn't. (b) In the wasm backend's string-concat lowering, when an operand's type is an unresolved generic, insert the runtime string-conversion (the same coercion used for `Int`/other → String in concat). Fix (a) is more general and also explains the native/wasm `+=` divergence; verify whether MIR carries the monomorphized type and the wasm backend is simply ignoring it.\n\n**Verify any fix against:** `/tmp/sbtest/Iso.hx` (all 5 rows), `/tmp/sbtest/Main.hx` (StringBuf add/addChar), and nue (restore `StringBuf` in `GenerationLoop` and confirm wasm streaming still works). Per [[feedback_nue_drives_compiler_fixes]] this is a compiler fix, not a Haxe workaround; the plain-String nue change is an interim unblock only. Also note `addChar` (non-generic, `b += String.fromCharCode(c)`) WORKS on wasm — consistent with the generic-operand-only theory.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_wasm_generic_string_concat` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}